<title>HONG KONG: HK's RNA shares debut at HK$1.32.</title>
<headline>HK's RNA shares debut at HK$1.32.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of RNA Holdings Ltd, a spin-off of the bullion and jewellery trader Tem Fat Hing Fung (Holdings) Ltd, made their trading debut at HK$1.32 per share in Hong Kong, compared with their issue price of HK$1.01 each.  </p>
<p>RNA offered 168 million shares at HK$1.01 per share. Its IPO was 30 times subscribed.</p>
<p>The company engages in refining, casting, assaying, wholesaling and trading of precious metals and related arbitrage and hedging operations.</p>
<p>It said net proceeds would be used to reduce bank borrowings, improve its management system and develop a gold and jewellery centre in Penang, Malaysia.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
